SUMMARY:Old-Fashioned Christmas & Small Business Saturday in Columbia
DESCRIPTION:Event Details & Schedule\n \n\n\n\nDate: Saturday\, November 28\, 2026\n\n \n\n\n\nLocation: Downtown Columbia\, PA & Columbia Market House / Locust Street Park\n\n \n\n\n\nSmall Business Saturday Shopping: Explore historic downtown storefronts adorned in traditional holiday decorations while supporting local merchants and eateries. [1\, 2]\n\n \n\n\n\nFamily Activities: Typically features family-friendly highlights such as cookie decorating\, a cocoa bar\, pictures with Santa and the Grinch (historically hosted at the Columbia Market House from 9:30 AM to 1:00 PM).\n\n \n\n\n\nEvening Festivities at Locust Street Park:\n\nCommunity Caroling: Featuring local church choirs.\nStorytime: Reading of ‘Twas the Night Before Christmas by Mrs. Claus.\nTree Lighting Ceremony: The official lighting of the borough’s Christmas tree.
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/old-fashioned-christmas-columbia/
LOCATION:Downtown Columbia\, 3rd & Locust Street\, Columbia\, PA\, 17512\, United States
CATEGORIES:Children & Family Events,Christmas - Visit Santa,Christmas Events in Lancaster County,Christmas Tree Lighting,Columbia PA,Community Interest,Entertainment,Food & Beverage Events,FREE Event,Holiday,Small Business Saturday,Winter
